{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sally's Health and Wellness Column", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "How About Some Yogurt?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe unusual events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Gerunds and Infinitives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"strong\">gerund </span>is a verb ending with <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>. Examples: <span class=\"italic\">doing</span>, <span class=\"italic\">watching</span>, <span class=\"italic\">talking</span>, <span class=\"italic\">playing</span>. <br/>An <span class=\"strong\">infinitive </span>  is when a verb is preceded by the word <span class=\"italic\">to</span>. Examples: <span class=\"italic\">to do</span>, <span class=\"italic\">to watch</span>, <span class=\"italic\">to talk</span>, <span class=\"italic\">to play</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Verbs commonly followed by a gerund:<br/>Verbs that express <span class=\"strong\">likes/dislikes</span>:<ul><li>like</li><li>love</li><li>enjoy</li><li>dislike</li><li>hate</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">Tom <span class=\"strong\">disliked eating</span> plain yogurt. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">like</span>/<span class=\"italic\">love</span>/<span class=\"italic\">hate</span> can also be followed by an infinitive.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Some other verbs that are followed by a gerund:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>anticipate</li><li>can't stand</li><li>delay</li><li>complete</li><li>involve</li><li>keep</li><li>risk</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These are some verbs that are followed by an infinitive:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>hope</li><li>proceed</li><li>seem</li><li>decide</li><li>help</li><li>happen</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">You should <span class=\"strong\">aim to eat</span> yogurt every day. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use Infinitives after adjectives. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">Yogurt is <span class=\"strong\">easy to make</span> at home. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These days supermarkets keep flooding their shelves with different kinds of yogurts in different flavors.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Yogurt helps to balance the healthy bacteria in the body, and it is also a good source of calcium. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Women's magazines claim that it even has qualities that happen to help the skin.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I don't know about you, but I can't stand eating plain yogurt!<br/> <br/>", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Be Supposed To </span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> to talk about situations in the past, present or future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure is:  <br/> <br/>Subject + <span class=\"italic\">To be</span> + <span class=\"italic\">supposed to</span> + verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">When it is applied directly on the skin, <span class=\"strong\">yogurt is supposed to heal</span> burns.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "**Pronunciation tip**: <br/>When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together. <br/> <br/> Like this: Be suppose_to", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To make it, a spoonful of existing yogurt is supposed to be put into a cup of milk.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The culture in the existing yogurt is supposed to react with the milk and in a few days yogurt is made. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Flavors are then supposed to be added to improve the taste. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fad ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a temporary fashion", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: But yogurt is not a new fad. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about yogurt.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "calcium ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an element in food that is important for many bodily functions", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Yogurt is a good source of calcium.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bacteria ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "microscopic organisms that live in animals and plants", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Yogurt helps to balance the healthy bacteria in the body.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "yogurt ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a milk-based food made with some bacteria", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Yogurt seems to have different qualities for your health.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "goat's milk", "type": "name"}, {"content": "milk from an animal similar to sheep", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Goat's milk yogurt was eaten a long time ago.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "yak ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a hairy animal similar to cows and bulls", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Genghis Khan ate a lot of yak milk yogurt.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "patriarch ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a man considered to be the founder of a social class", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Patriarch Abraham ate goat's milk yogurt.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "biblical ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "related to the Bible", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Methuselah, King Solomon and Abraham are biblical characters.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fermented ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that experienced a chemical change because of the action of yeast or bacteria", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Yogurt is fermented from milk and live cultures.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob05aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "live culture", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a group of bacteria that has been grown in a scientific experiment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Yogurt is supposed to be made from live cultures.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob05aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"